---
import { siteConfig } from '../data/siteConfig';
---

<section class="bento-section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="features-title">Engineered for Linux Developers</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Google publishes standalone archives without Linux repositories. We bridge that gap with enterprise-grade packaging infrastructure.</p>

  <div class="bento-grid">
    <div class="bento-card">
      <span class="bento-icon" aria-hidden="true">📦</span>
      <h3>Real Package Management</h3>
      <p>Direct integration with <code>dnf</code>, <code>apt</code>, and <code>zypper</code>. No dumping files into <code>/opt</code>, no manual tarball extractions, and clean uninstalls.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento-card">
      <span class="bento-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚡</span>
      <h3>Daily Upstream Sync</h3>
      <p>Automated daily CI/CD pipeline tracks Google's official release CDN at 05:00 UTC. Releases are tested in Fedora and Ubuntu containers before publishing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento-card">
      <span class="bento-icon" aria-hidden="true">📂</span>
      <h3>Multi-Desktop Right-Click</h3>
      <p>Native context menus for GNOME Files (Nautilus), KDE (Dolphin), Linux Mint (Nemo), MATE (Caja), and COSMIC Desktop to instantly <strong>Open in Antigravity IDE</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento-card">
      <span class="bento-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔐</span>
      <h3>Cryptographically Signed</h3>
      <p>All RPM repodata, APT releases, and binaries are signed with the official <code>{siteConfig.gpg.maintainer.split('<')[0].trim()}</code> GPG key (Fingerprint: <code>{siteConfig.gpg.fingerprint}</code>).</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
